  <section>
    <h2>Hidden Greens — Buxton medical cannabis store</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 370 Narragansett Trail, Buxton, ME 04093<br />
      <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+12072989111">(207) 298-9111</a><br />
      <strong>Official location page:</strong> <a href="https://hiddengreens.com/buxton/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hiddengreens.com/buxton</a><br />
      <strong>Program advertised by operator:</strong> Medical</p>
    <p>The official Buxton page lists flower, pre-rolls, edibles, concentrates, beverages, and other medical-cannabis products. It does not publish store hours. Call the number above or use the operator's current menu before making a trip; do not rely on hours copied from an older directory.</p>
    <p>The company homepage also links a delivery menu, but it does not establish that the Buxton storefront itself performs every delivery or define a service area. Confirm the responsible registered caregiver or dispensary, patient requirements, destination, and current availability before ordering. Maine does not issue a general medical cannabis courier license.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Important OCP registry context</h2>
    <p>OCP's <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/open-data/medical-use/registrant-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medical Use Applicant and Registrant Search</a> says its downloadable data was last updated July 8, 2026 and reflects a June 1, 2026 file date.</p>
    <p>OCP's medical-establishment snapshot lists active medical dispensary registration <strong>DSP159</strong> under <strong>Caberski Industries LLC</strong>, DBA <strong>Hidden Greens</strong>, with Buxton as the license city. That state record connects Hidden Greens to an active Buxton medical dispensary registration.</p>
    <p>The establishment snapshot does not publish a street address, so the operator's official page remains the primary source for the advertised 370 Narragansett Trail location. OCP's separate caregiver file also lists The Corner Store (CGR28664) with Buxton as retail town and Caberski Industries/Hidden Greens caregiver registration CGR26972 with South Berwick as retail town. Those are separate caregiver registrations; they do not negate the Buxton dispensary record DSP159.</p>
    <Callout title="How to read the records" type="info">
      The operator page supplies the advertised street address, while OCP's establishment file confirms an active Hidden Greens dispensary registration in Buxton. Because the state snapshot does not include a street address, verify DSP159 in OCP's live search and confirm the responsible registration before a transaction or delivery.
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Buxton's current ordinance says</h2>
    <p>Buxton's June 14, 2025 zoning ordinance expressly regulates medical cannabis:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Districts:</strong> Article 9 lists “Medical Marijuana Dispensaries” as conditional uses in the Business/Commercial and Light Commercial districts and as not permitted in the other listed districts.</li>
      <li><strong>Cap:</strong> Section 11.27.1 limits registered dispensaries to three within the town.</li>
      <li><strong>Buffer:</strong> Section 11.27.2 requires at least 500 feet, property line to property line, from schools, libraries, playgrounds, parks, houses of worship, and daycares.</li>
      <li><strong>Size:</strong> The section limits the facility to 2,500 square feet.</li>
      <li><strong>Hours:</strong> It allows operation from 8:00 a.m. to 9:00 p.m., Monday through Sunday. Those are the municipal outer limits, not proof of an operator's actual posted hours.</li>
      <li><strong>Operations:</strong> The ordinance addresses indoor cultivation, alarms, exterior lighting, surveillance, and odor control for registered dispensaries and associated cultivation facilities.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Section 11.30 separately governs medical marijuana caregiver/home-occupation activity. It requires patient distribution in an enclosed building, prohibits drive-through or window service, and limits dispensing to 7:00 a.m.–8:00 p.m. for the caregiver/home-occupation category. Which section applies depends on the operator's actual registration and municipal approval.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Adult-use status</h2>
    <p>OCP's <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/open-data/adult-use/licensee-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adult-use establishment file</a>, updated on OCP's page July 8, 2026 with a June 1 file date, contains no Buxton applicant or licensee row. Buxton's cited zoning provisions address medical dispensaries and caregiver activity; they do not establish an approved adult-use cannabis store.</p>
    <p>Adults may possess cannabis under Maine law, but an adult-use retail sale must come from an active adult-use cannabis store licensee. Verify current state data before relying on a nearby listing.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Patient checklist before visiting</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm the store is open; the operator's Buxton page does not publish hours.</li>
      <li>Ask which active medical-program registrant is responsible for the Buxton sale.</li>
      <li>Verify that registrant through OCP's live licensing search or downloadable data.</li>
      <li>Bring current government identification and the medical documentation required for your patient status.</li>
      <li>If visiting from another state, review OCP's <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/medical-use/visiting-patients" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">visiting-patient guidance</a> before traveling.</li>
      <li>Confirm product availability, payment methods, return policy, and delivery responsibility directly with the operator.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

